From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Subject: wifi: ath11k: walk only the set-up tx rings on mac stop

ath11k_dp_tx_complete_pending() (911) walks DP_TCL_NUM_RING_MAX tx rings,
but ath11k_dp_alloc() initialises the tx_idr_lock and the idr pool only
for hal_params->num_tx_rings of them. Taking the lock of a ring that was
never set up makes lockdep report a non-static key and switch itself
off, here when hostapd stops an IPQ5018 radio with NSS disabled. Walk
the rings that were set up.

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.c
@@ -1070,7 +1070,7 @@ void ath11k_dp_tx_complete_pending(struc
 	struct sk_buff *msdu;
 	int i, j;
 
-	for (i = 0; i < DP_TCL_NUM_RING_MAX; i++) {
+	for (i = 0; i < ab->hw_params.hal_params->num_tx_rings; i++) {
 		struct dp_tx_ring *tx_ring = &dp->tx_ring[i];
 
 		spin_lock_bh(&tx_ring->tx_idr_lock);
